 ### Adaptive Range Coding
-Adaptive Range Coding is a lossless entropy coding technique using range coding with adaptive probability models [S1]. The encoder and decoder start from the same fixed initial model and update symbol frequencies online as the stream is encoded/decoded, avoiding explicit histogram transmission [S1]. This approach avoids the per-stream metadata overhead and complexity associated with explicit model approaches (building histograms and transmitting tables) when many short streams are produced [S1].
+Adaptive Range Coding is a lossless entropy coding technique using range coding with adaptive probability models [S1]. The encoder and decoder start from the same fixed initial model and update symbol frequencies online as the stream is encoded or decoded, avoiding explicit histogram transmission [S1]. This approach avoids the per-stream metadata overhead and complexity associated with explicit model approaches when many short streams are produced [S1].
 
